<section class="cs-hero container">
    <figure class="sx-cover"><img src="../assets/images/study-buddy.png" alt="Study Buddy project artwork" width="1200" height="600"></figure>
      
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="../index.html">De La Paz</a> / <a href="../index.html#work">Work</a> / Study Buddy</div>
    <h1>Study Buddy</h1>
    <p class="tagline">A desktop focus companion. A small mascot, Mambo, runs your study sessions and asks for breaks with friendly overlays instead of locking your screen. I designed it in Figma, then built it by directing AI and reviewing every round myself.</p>
    <div class="impact-grid cs-glance"><div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">~14 hrs</div><div class="l">active build time, from commit timestamps</div></div><div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">40+</div><div class="l">commits, every round reviewed by me</div></div><div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">3</div><div class="l">desktop installers: Windows, Mac, Linux</div></div></div>
    <div class="cs-badge-row">
      <span>Desktop App (Windows / Mac / Linux)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-action-row">
      <a href="https://github.com/EricArielDeLaPaz/study-buddy-desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>View GitHub Repository <svg class="sx-btn-icon" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 22v-4a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1-3.5c3 0 6-2 6-5.5.08-1.25-.27-2.48-1-3.5.28-1.15.28-2.35 0-3.5 0 0-1 0-3 1.5-2.64-.5-5.36-.5-8 0C6 2 5 2 5 2c-.3 1.15-.3 2.35 0 3.5A5.403 5.403 0 0 0 4 9c0 3.5 3 5.5 6 5.5-.39.49-.68 1.05-.85 1.65-.17.6-.22 1.23-.15 1.85v4"/><path d="M9 18c-4.51 2-5-2-7-2"/></svg></span></a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/eric-ariel-de-la-paz_uxdesign-productdesign-studentlife-ugcPost-7517057393239752704-cLUV/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAFwSUJgBsQv-5MDGy8Lu7UaL4Oxsc64LZLc" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>View LinkedIn Overlay Demo <svg class="sx-btn-icon" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="6 3 20 12 6 21 6 3"/></svg></span></a>
    </div>
    <dl class="cs-meta">
      <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Product designer, AI-assisted builder</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>In progress, rolling updates</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Desktop first, mobile next</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tools</dt><dd>Figma, Gemini 4 Argon</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-body container">
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>Structure without the pressure</h2>
      <p>Focus and break timers, water reminders, and blockers, delivered in a friendlier way.</p>
      <div class="reasoning-chain compact">
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">I noticed</span>
          <span class="v">I drifted to YouTube during my own study sessions and wanted help focusing and managing my time.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">So I designed</span>
          <span class="v">An ambient companion that floats over your work with timers, reminders and nudges. Postpone a break in one tap (+30s, +1m, +5m); the window tucks away for full screen.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">Evaluated via</span>
          <span class="v">Dogfooding: I use it daily in my own study sessions, and every round is run and clicked through before the next change list.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>Designed in Figma first</h2>
      <p>Session, reminders, schedule, app rules, progress, buddy screens, break overlays, and the Mambo widget, in light and dark themes on shared tokens (Fredoka, DM Sans).</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-row cols-2">
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-session.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-session.png" alt="Figma design of the Study Buddy session screen" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Figma: the session screen, with presets, a study goal and the Mambo preview.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-buddy-studio.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-buddy-studio.png" alt="Figma design of the Buddy Studio screen with presets and animation slots" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Figma: Buddy Studio, where each animation is linked to a session, reminder or alert.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>From frame to working overlay</h2>
      <p>The break overlay is the heart of the product: a calm card with a small plus to postpone. Figma held a placeholder; the build plays Mambo's states, with a gentler nudge for distracting sites.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-row cols-3">
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-overlay-hydration.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/figma-overlay-hydration.png" alt="Figma frame of the hydration break overlay with a placeholder character" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Design: hydration break in Figma.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-overlay-hydration.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-overlay-hydration.png" alt="Built hydration break overlay with the Mambo character" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Built: the same break with Mambo.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-overlay-intervention.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-overlay-intervention.png" alt="Built distraction nudge overlay asking whether to keep or close a distracting app" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Built: the nudge, shown when you open a listed app or site during a focus session.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>Working with AI, on purpose</h2>
      <p>I directed the AI and kept the product decisions. Each round followed one loop.</p>
      <div class="reasoning-chain is-row compact">
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">I designed</span>
          <span class="v">Frames, tokens and reference screenshots in Figma. Every round starts by comparing the running app to them.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">I directed</span>
          <span class="v">I wrote each change in plain language; Gemini structured it into a prompt, and Gemini 4 Argon generated the Electron, React and TypeScript.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chain-step">
          <span class="k">I reviewed</span>
          <span class="v">I ran the app, clicked every screen, and wrote the next change list. Saved transcripts show 10 rounds (stages 9 to 18).</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">~14 hrs</div><div class="l">active build time, from commit timestamps</div></div>
        <div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">40+</div><div class="l">commits</div></div>
        <div class="impact-stat"><div class="n">~15k</div><div class="l">lines of TypeScript and React</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <div class="cs-split" style="--split:1.25fr">
        <div class="cs-split-text">
          <h2>Dogfooding and edge-case elimination</h2>
          <p>I run the app myself every day, then write the next change list from what breaks, confuses, or feels unfinished. Fixes from those rounds:</p>
          <ul><li>Cut clutter: the Messages tab and a focus-timer pill</li><li>Made the window behave like a normal app: resizable, no fullscreen, close tucks into Mambo</li><li>Fixed low-contrast light-mode text against WCAG AA (formal audit still to do)</li><li>One purple palette instead of blue and purple, with hover states on every desktop button</li><li>Confirmation dialogs before delete, clear and sign-out actions</li><li>Removed settings that did not work yet (cloud sync, "iPhone connected")</li></ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-split-media">
          <div class="cs-figure-row cols-1 sm">
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-session-dark.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-session-dark.png" alt="Study Buddy session screen in dark theme" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Dark theme.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-session-light.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-session-light.png" alt="Study Buddy session screen in light theme" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Light theme, after the contrast pass.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>The desktop app</h2>
      <p>Editable reminders, a schedule for study blocks, and app rules that nudge you when a listed app or site opens mid-session. Auto-starting sessions from the schedule is next.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-row cols-3">
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-reminders.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-reminders.png" alt="Reminders screen with editable reminder cards" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Reminders.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-schedule.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-schedule.png" alt="Schedule screen with study time blocks" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Schedule.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-app-rules.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-app-rules.png" alt="App rules screen listing apps and sites that trigger a nudge" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>App rules.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>Companions and progress</h2>
      <p>Mambo is the starting companion; levels unlock more, and each companion's animations can link to a reminder, session or alert. A progress screen tracks focus hours, streaks and level.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-row cols-2">
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-buddy-studio.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-buddy-studio.png" alt="Buddy Studio screen with companions and animation slots" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Buddy Studio.</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><a class="cs-zoom" href="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-progress.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full size"><img src="../assets/images/case-studies/study-buddy/app-progress.png" alt="Progress screen with focus hours, streak and companion level" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Progress. Numbers shown are sample data.</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-section">
      <h2>What's next</h2>
      <p>Rolling updates, desktop first.</p>
      <ul><li><strong>Keep dogfooding:</strong> daily use and more edge-case sweeps on every release</li><li><strong>Smart activation:</strong> opening a study app or site starts Mambo and a session (list saved, auto-start not built)</li><li><strong>Mobile app, accounts and sync:</strong> planned, not built</li><li><strong>Formal accessibility check</strong> of both themes</li></ul>
    </div>
  </section>

